# The Dataset is a build gate, so nothing under it may ever be ignored (§11).
# `!data/` comes first: git never descends into an ignored directory. Only the
# last matching pattern counts, so these win against any broad rule added *above*
# them and lose to one appended below -- which is why the actual guard is the
# gate's own ignore check (`cargo run -p bench -- verify`, and the test
# `nothing_under_the_dataset_is_ignored`). Never `git add -f` a Dataset file: it
# hides the pattern that will eat the next archive.
!data/
!data/dataset/
!data/dataset/**
